d2d1: Write each draw's constant data to a reused buffer bound with offsets.

Every primitive mapped the vertex and pixel shader constant buffers with
WRITE_DISCARD, which makes wined3d rename them: a new allocation for each
buffer on every draw. Append the data to one dynamic constant buffer per
device context instead, mapped NO_OVERWRITE (DISCARD when it wraps), and
bind the draw's slices with VSSetConstantBuffers1 and
PSSetConstantBuffers1. Direct3D 11.1's constant buffer offsets and
no-overwrite maps of dynamic constant buffers are both supported by Wine's
d3d11.

The d2d1 conformance tests give the same result before and after (17491
tests, 0 failures). In Affinity under a nested KWin, on top of 0055, three
rounds each, CPU per presented frame on wined3d's command thread and the
UI thread:

                 before          after
  drag         6.0 / 10.3 ms   5.6 /  9.7 ms
  node edit    5.7 /  9.0 ms   5.3 /  8.8 ms
  zoom         7.7 / 10.7 ms   7.5 / 10.3 ms
  typing       4.3 / 20.7 ms   3.9 / 20.1 ms

